videotoolbox: hand out BGRA for >8-bit 4:2:0 on iOS

iOS's OpenGL ES has no 16-bit normalized texture formats, so the P010
frames VideoToolbox returns for 10-bit HEVC cannot be mapped by mpv's
ios-gl interop ("Format unsupported"): 10-bit hardware decoding would
fail or show nothing. On iOS, ask VideoToolbox for BGRA instead (it
converts), and let BGRA be mapped from a video-range stream too.

Carried over from media-kit's libmpv-darwin-build
(patches/ffmpeg-fix-ios-hdr-texture.patch, v0.7.3); the comments are
theirs. Rebased onto FFmpeg n8.1.3 with exact context (the original
needed an offset and fuzz). Darwin only: the Android build does not use
VideoToolbox. Kept until an iPhone A/B shows that the app setting
hwdec-image-format=nv12 can replace it (plynic spec 0017 M0-4, TD19).

diff --git a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
index 2cd22cb..901903e 100644
--- a/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavcodec/videotoolbox.c
@@ -1225,7 +1225,12 @@ static enum AVPixelFormat videotoolbox_best_pixel_format(AVCodecContext *avctx)
 #endif
 #if HAVE_KCVPIXELFORMATTYPE_420YPCBCR10BIPLANARVIDEORANGE
     if (depth > 8) {
+#if TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+        // @tmm1: iOS doesn't support 10 bit textures in GLES.
+        return AV_PIX_FMT_BGRA;
+#else
         return AV_PIX_FMT_P010;
+#endif
     }
 #endif
 
diff --git a/libavutil/hwcontext_videotoolbox.c b/libavutil/hwcontext_videotoolbox.c
index 2764097..91ce23b 100644
--- a/libavutil/hwcontext_videotoolbox.c
+++ b/libavutil/hwcontext_videotoolbox.c
@@ -49,7 +49,10 @@ static const struct {
     { kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8Planar,              false, AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P },
     { kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8PlanarFullRange,     true,  AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P },
     { kCVPixelFormatType_422YpCbCr8,                    false, AV_PIX_FMT_UYVY422 },
-    { kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA,                        true,  AV_PIX_FMT_BGRA },
+    // @alexmercerind: |kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA| must be available without full range, otherwise
+    // |av_map_videotoolbox_format_from_pixfmt2| will be unable to map it (due to change in
+    // |videotoolbox_best_pixel_format|) & H/W acceleration will fail.
+    { kCVPixelFormatType_32BGRA,                        false,  AV_PIX_FMT_BGRA },
 #ifdef kCFCoreFoundationVersionNumber10_7
     { kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8BiPlanarVideoRange,  false, AV_PIX_FMT_NV12 },
     { kCVPixelFormatType_420YpCbCr8BiPlanarFullRange,   true,  AV_PIX_FMT_NV12 },
